cyberpunk 2077's secret editions are  starting to be discovered no man's sky's  newest expansion is out now and more  during cd projekt red's 1.5 patch reveal  stream it was also mentioned that there  would be some new secrets for players to  discover throughout the game including  one that only three developers know  about and a few of them are starting to  surface user rogue taco art on reddit  shared a clip of a cop vs gang shootout  showcasing the new interactions between  the npcs in night city and this is just  the tip of the iceberg as there have  also been videos of full out npc police  chases caught on cam there are also a  few quality of life changes that weren't  listed in the patch notes such as being  able to skip the braindance tutorial new  photo mode poses inspired by anime and  various balance changes that some fans  are saying it makes the game feel more  like an rpg aside from new secrets being  discovered it has been really fun seeing  everyone share the before and after  photos of their characters and seeing  just how much better they look in patch  1.5 i'm sure we're going to see a lot  more discoveries in night city in the  coming weeks but what are some of your  favorite changes in the game so far  no man's sky is a game that has been no  stranger to updates ever since it  initially launched in 2016. this time  around developer hello games has offered  players the sentinel update the update  features even more of what they want to  see with a complete combat overhaul the  ability to have their own drones to take  care of and more  announced alongside its release the  sentinel update is also going to allow  players to have their own mech friend by  letting the xo mek take the form of a  full on robot with the use of an ai core  not only this but the update includes an  overhaul of the weapons system even more  lore and brand new sentinel enemies with  new combat behavior and while the  sentinel update may be the 19th  expansion coming to no man's sky hello  games is nowhere near the end of its  development life cycle sean murray says  the team is continuously thinking of new  content to add and that the list of  things the team is excited about never  gets any shorter nintendo has open  registrations for the nintendo switch  sports online play test also advising  players that they are strictly forbidden  from sharing any footage the online play  test runs this weekend on february 19th  and 20th for a set period of hours each  day and you need to be a subscriber to  nintendo's switch online membership to  get in nintendo clarified that the  online test represents an in-development  version of the game so players might  encounter some unexpected behaviors or  errors while playing additionally save  data from the test does not carry  forward to the full launch in april and  the test will not run on switch light  consoles what's more is nintendo said  those accepted into the test are not  allowed to share any details from their  experiences these restrictions are not  uncommon for pre-release tests but it's  also not always the rule recently sony  announced that everyone in mlb the show  22's tech test can share all the footage  that they want nintendo is holding this  test to make sure certain technical  aspects of the game hold up at launch  players will get to try out online  tennis bowling and more to get into the  nintendo switch sports test visit the  websites linked in the description to  begin the process  it involves signing into your nintendo  account and redeeming a 16-digit code  supplied to you  have you found any other new secrets in  cyberpunk 2077 let me know in the  comments and of course leave a like  subscribe and come back tomorrow for  another episode of gamespot news see you  later  [Music]
 

